      "description": "Rue de la Gare, at the corner of Avenue du Marsupilami. 11 a.m.\nBob Hermann, 32, wearing a leather jacket that still smells brand new and a 1914 aviator helmet, has just discovered that his yellow Triumph doubles as a flamb\u00e9ed-cr\u00eape machine.\nRear brake locked, smoking rubber, sparks flying like a Bastille Day fireworks display, and a skid mark as long as an overbaked baguette. The light is red. Kevin couldn't care less. He\u2019s in the middle of a riding demonstration for the local bakery.\nRetired duo Dupont and Dupond: \"SIR, YOU\u2019RE GOING TO DIE.\"\nThey aren't even looking at the motorcycle. They\u2019re gazing at the croissants gleaming in the shop window. It\u2019s the ultimate dilemma: rescue the young man or take advantage of the open bakery door to swipe the last *pain au chocolat*.\nFurther back, at the Caf\u00e9 des Incapables, nobody moves.",
